 "text": "Comparing China and India by Economy - StatisticsTimes.com\n\n# Comparing China and India by Economy\n\n| Source | World Bank : Nominal, PPP, Nominal per capita, PPP per capita |\n| --- | --- |\n| | International Monetary Fund World Economic Outlook (October - 2025) |\n| Date | 06 Mar 2026 |\n\nTop Statistics\n\nList of continents by gdp per capita\n\nTop 10 largest economies by GDP\n\n- See Also:\n- » India vs China population\n- » United States vs China by Economy\n- » India vs Pakistan by Economy\n- View More Economy Statistics\n\nChina and India are the two emerging economies in the world. As of 2025, China and India are the 2nd and 5th largest economies in the world, respectively, on a nominal basis. On a PPP basis, China is in 1st place, and India is in 3rd. Both countries share 20.08% and 28.11% of the total global wealth in nominal and PPP terms, respectively. Among Asian countries, China and India together contribute 55.6% in nominal and 57.1% in PPP of Asia's GDP.\n\nIn 1987, the GDP (nominal) of both countries was almost equal; even in PPP terms, China was slightly ahead of India in 1990. Now in 2025, China's GDP of $19,399 billion is 4.58 times higher than India's$4,125 billion. On a PPP basis, the GDP of China (Int. $41,016 billion) is 2.27x that of India (Int. $17,714 billion). China crossed the $1 trillion mark in 1998, while India crossed it nine years later in 2007 on an exchange rate basis.\n\nBoth countries have been neck-and-neck in GDP per capita terms till 1991. As per both methods, India was richer than China in 1990. In 2025, China ($13,806) is almost 4.83 times richer than India ($2,818) on the nominal and 2.39 times richer in the ppp method. The per capita rank of China and India is 78th and 146th, respectively, in nominal terms. The per capita rank of China and India is 79th and 127th, respectively, in PPP.\n\nChina attains a maximum GDP growth rate of 19.30% in 1970 and a minimum of -27.27% in 1961. India reached an all-time high of 9.69% in 2021 and a record low of -5.78% in 2020. From 1961 to 2024, China grew by more than 10% in 22 years, while India never did. GDP growth rate was negative in five years for both China and India.\n\n- GDP\n- GDP per capita\n- GDP growth\n\nProjections by IMF\n\n| Year | Nominal GDP (billions $) | | PPP GDP (billions Int. $) | | Nominal GDP capita ($) | | PPP GDP capita (Int. $) | | Growth (%) | |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| | China | India | China | India | China | India | China | India | China | India |\n| 2024 | 18,749.759 | 3,909.892 | 38,209.549 | 16,215.925 | 13,314 | 2,695 | 27,132 | 11,176 | 5.003 | 6.495 |\n| 2025 | 19,398.577 | 4,125.213 | 41,015.824 | 17,714.186 | 13,806 | 2,818 | 29,191 | 12,101 | 4.796 | 6.646 |\n| 2026 | 20,650.754 | 4,505.629 | 43,491.52 | 19,143.371 | 14,730 | 3,051 | 31,023 | 12,964 | 4.163 | 6.159 |\n| 2027 | 22,016.582 | 4,958.953 | 46,072.056 | 20,711.997 | 15,741 | 3,330 | 32,939 | 13,908 | 4.186 | 6.409 |\n| 2028 | 23,451.376 | 5,461.673 | 48,676.822 | 22,412.554 | 16,809 | 3,638 | 34,889 | 14,927 | 3.965 | 6.481 |\n| 2029 | 24,852.392 | 6,015.999 | 51,361.78 | 24,286.192 | 17,862 | 3,975 | 36,914 | 16,047 | 3.700 | 6.495 |\n| 2030 | 26,336.991 | 6,627.982 | 54,084.435 | 26,350.976 | 18,985 | 4,346 | 38,986 | 17,278 | 3.362 | 6.504 |\n\nEstimates by World Bank\n\n| Year | Nominal GDP (billions $) | | PPP GDP (billions Int. $) | | Nominal GDP capita ($) | | PPP GDP capita (Int. $) | | Growth (%) | |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| | China | India | China | India | China | India | China | India | China | India |\n| 1960 | 59.85 | 37.03 | - | - | 90 | 85 | - | - | - | - |\n| 1961 | 50.16 | 39.23 | - | - | 76 | 88 | - | - | -27.27 | 3.72 |\n| 1962 | 47.31 | 42.16 | - | - | 71 | 92 | - | - | -5.58 | 2.93 |\n| 1963 | 50.81 | 48.42 | - | - | 74 | 103 | - | - | 10.30 | 5.99 |\n| 1964 | 59.82 | 56.48 | - | - | 86 | 118 | - | - | 18.18 | 7.45 |\